T* (  The optical system of the camera is a modified Ritchey-Chretien design with correc-                                             ) Tj
T* (ting field lens \(Fig. 1\). The telescope is mounted behind the spacecraft bumper shield                                            ) Tj
T* (and therefore protected from direct dust-particle impacts. A 45deg deflecting mirror is                                           ) Tj
T* (used to look at the comet. A baffle ensures adequate reduction of diffuse sunlight and                                            ) Tj
T* (spacecraft-reflected light.                                                                                                       ) Tj
T* (  The telescope images onto a focal-plane arrangement of one reticon and two area                                                 ) Tj
T* (CCDs \(Charge-Coupled Devices\). The reticon is used to detect the nucleus and later                                                ) Tj
T* (to clock the two area CCDs. The area CCDs are used in a mode in which only a few                                                  ) Tj
T* (active lines scan the image of the comet during its apparent motion across the rotating                                           ) Tj
T* (\(because of the spacecraft spin\) field of view; the remaining lines are masked and used                                           ) Tj
T* (as a low-power˘ highly efficient data buffer. The contents of the exposed lines are                                               ) Tj
T* (shifted into the masked CCD lines at precisely the same rate as the nucleus image                                                 ) Tj
T* (moves. Using CCDs as the intermediate storage for a line scanner allows exposure                                                  ) Tj
T* (times as short as 10 micro s to be used. Smear due to the spinning motion of the camera                                           ) Tj
T* (is then negligible, even for the detector's high resolution of 22 microrad per pixel. In the                                      ) Tj
T* (nucleus-imaging mode, the camera works best if the nucleus is slightly \(>~ 1deg\) off spin                                         ) Tj
T* (axis. The two area CCDs each have two segments, three of the four segments being                                                  ) Tj
T* (tinted to provide colour pictures.                                                                                                ) Tj
T* (                                                                                                                                  ) Tj
