T* (2.3 The Ion Mass Spectrometer \(IMS\)                                                                                               ) Tj
T* (  The Ion Mass Spectrometer is made up of two sensors, a High-Energy Range Spec-                                                  ) Tj
T* (trometer \(HERS\) optimized for measurements in the outer coma where a turbulent                                                    ) Tj
T* (transition between solar wind and cometary ions is expected, and a High-Intensity                                                 ) Tj
T* (Spectrometer \(HIS\) optimized for measurements in the inner coma where high fluxes                                                 ) Tj
T* (of relatively cold cometary ions are anticipated.                                                                                 ) Tj
T* (  The HERS sensor \(Fig. 3\) consists basically of an electrostatic mirror to deflect the                                           ) Tj
T* (cometary ions into the instrument, a pair of grids with variable applied voltage, a sec-                                          ) Tj
T* (tor magnet which serves as momentum-per-charge filter, and an electrostatic deflector                                             ) Tj
T* (which spreads the momentum-analyzed ions according to their energy per charge. The                                                ) Tj
T* (beam is then imaged onto a two-dimensional microchannel plate, with one dimension                                                 ) Tj
T* (a measure of mass-per-charge, and the other a measure of the elevation angle of the                                               ) Tj
T* (ion's velocity vector. Azimuth angle is scanned via the spacecraft's spin and the                                                 ) Tj
T* (energy distribution is determined by variation of the voltages applied to the pair of                                             ) Tj
T* (grids.                                                                                                                            ) Tj
T* (                                                                                                                                  ) Tj
T* ( The HIS sensor \(Fig. 4\) employs two quadrispherical electrostatic analyzers with                                                 ) Tj
T* (magnetic deflection and an array of 4 X4 channeltrons as detectors. The energy-per-                                               ) Tj
T* (charge of the particles to be analyzed is selected by the differential voltage applied to                                         ) Tj
T* (the first electrostatic analyzer, while the momentum-per-charge \(and thus mass-per-                                               ) Tj
T* (charge\) is determined by the acceleration potential applied between a pair of plane                                               ) Tj
T* (parallel grids located behind the exit of that analyzer. The ion species expected at the                                          ) Tj
T* (selected energy is imaged at the centre of the one-dimensional detector array of four                                             ) Tj
T* (channeltrons. Hence, the mass spectrum and the temperatures of all individual species                                             ) Tj
T* (can be measured by just scanning through the energy-per-charge range. The other                                                   ) Tj
T* (direction of the channeltron array provides resolution in elevation, while azimuth                                                ) Tj
T* (angle is scanned by the spacecraft spin.                                                                                          ) Tj
T* (                                                                                                                                  ) Tj
