T* (2.11 The Magnetometer \(MAG\)                                                                                                       ) Tj
T* (  The magnetic field is to be measured by a wide-range \(0.004-65536 nT\) triaxial                                                  ) Tj
T* (ring-core fluxgate magnetometer mounted on the antenna tripod, where it is furthest                                               ) Tj
T* (from the spacecraft and also protected from dust impacts \(Fig. 15\). The Giotto                                                    ) Tj
T* (magnetometer is identical to the GSFC fluxgate magnetometers carried on Voyager                                                   ) Tj
T* (and destined for flight on ESA's Ulysses \(formerly ISPM\) spacecraft. Noise                                                        ) Tj
T* (characteristics have been improved by use of different sensor core alloys.                                                        ) Tj
T* (  The principle of the fluxgate magnetometer is as follows \(Fig. 12\). Suppose that in                                             ) Tj
T* (the simplest sensor arrangement a ferromagnetic core of soft magnetic material is                                                 ) Tj
T* (periodically driven into saturation by a drive coil generating a periodic magnetic field                                          ) Tj
T* (strength of suitable wave shape at the drive frequence f\(0\). An additional sense coil                                             ) Tj
T* (around the core will then exhibit a distorted signal composed of frequency components                                             ) Tj
T* (at f\(0\) and odd harmonics. Addition of an ambient magnetic-field component along the                                              ) Tj
T* (core axis will lead to the appearance of even harmonics. Generally, in fluxgate                                                   ) Tj
T* (magnetometers the second harmonic is detected because its amplitude turns out to be                                               ) Tj
T* (proportional to the ambient field component parallel to the core or the sense-coil axis.                                          ) Tj
T* (To obtain good linearity, a feedback coil is generally added to compensate the ambient                                            ) Tj
T* (magnetic field in response to the output from the sense coil. In this case, the sense                                             ) Tj
T* (coil is essentially used for zero detection only.                                                                                 ) Tj
T* (  The measurement of the ambient magnetic field is disturbed by the spacecraft field,                                             ) Tj
T* (which generally has two sources: perm fields and induced fields due to magnetic                                                   ) Tj
T* (materials, and stray fields due to varying electric currents. Because of their potential                                          ) Tj
T* (lack of stability, magnetically soft materials are particularly disturbing for magnetic                                           ) Tj
T* (measurements. The same is true for stray fields. Major sources of contamination are:                                              ) Tj
T* (the antenna despin motor, the NMS and IMS experiment magnets, the three HMC                                                       ) Tj
T* (motors and the PIA motor, the HMC invar, the antenna feed, the TWTs and the lat-                                                  ) Tj
T* (ching relays. Present estimates indicate a combined experiment/spacecraft field                                                   ) Tj
T* (strength of ~ 30 nT, with ~ 10% variability at the location of the outer sensor.                                                  ) Tj
T* (  The magnetometer has two sensors, an outboard sensor located about 1.1 m above                                                  ) Tj
T* (the upper face of the spacecraft body, and an inboard sensor located about 0.5 m above                                            ) Tj
